    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 11,
      "text": "In the meantime, the order dated 31.08.2022 passed by Mr Praveen Kumar Malviya, SDJM,\nKatihar in CA No 2089 of 2019, whereby cognizance of offences under Sections 420, Patna High Court CR. MISC. No.31216 of 2023(2) dt.19-10-2023 406, 498A and 34 of IPC read with Sections 3 and 4 of Dowry Prohibition Act has been taken, shall remain stayed as it has been submitted that petitioner was married to Opposite Party No 2 by deceit for which he had filed a case under Section 11 of the Hindu Marriage Act in the Court of the Additional Principal Judge, Family Court, Deoghar Amit Sinha vs The State Of Bihar on 19 October, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/80741734/\n1 for declaring the marriage null and void, wherein a compromise was entered into between the parties and Opposite Party No 2 had undertaken to withdraw the present case.",
